# Written fresh by .claude/hooks/session-start.sh on every session: which
# python modules are present, how much disk is left, which branch is checked
# out. It is a snapshot of one machine at one moment, so committing it would
# put a stale environment into everyone else's checkout and churn on every
# branch. The `.local` in the name is the signal — it stays out of the repo.
.claude/env-facts.local.md
